7. THE VOTE PATH'S IN-SERVICE SELF-TEST, RESTATED IN ROUND 9 (W143, on W139's analysis in T10-CANQ.md; specified for the firmware stage,
   its contract text in apply_hw_fw_contract_canq.py; nothing applied). Round 7's schedule is SUPERSEDED: its precondition read as worded
   never runs an S phase (W139-F5), its V phase commands the votes so the attribution path is never exercised (W139-F8), and it stops
   testing whenever one fabric is down. The restated schedule is W139's (W139-D1 to D3), with its words made exact here:
   THE WINDOW (100 ms on each fabric, FW-B22 restated): the state slots A 10, B 20 and C 30 ms, 10 ms each, are never touched by the test;
     the test acts only in its own segment, the hold 52 to 88 ms, where each controller sends one test frame (A at 60, B at 70, C at 80 ms)
   THE CYCLE (12 windows): in window n the target on fabric A is A, B or C by (n mod 12) div 4 and on fabric B the next controller, and
     the phase is S, P1, P2 or V by n mod 4; both fabrics are tested at once, so each of the six transceivers meets each phase once a cycle:
     S  its own SHDN request over the hold: its test frame received by no peer, and it hears no peer's -> silenced
     P1 the next controller's vote alone over the hold (commanded): every test frame received both ways -> not
        silenced
     P2 the one after's vote alone over the hold (commanded): every test frame received both ways -> not silenced
     V  its ONE malformed test frame (12 dominant bit-times, V1) at the hold's start, struck by both readers through
        their attribution paths; their votes act to the hold's end and it hears no peer's test frame -> silenced
   THE PRECONDITION, per fabric (as worded, and run here literally): in the previous window every controller received every other
     controller's STATE frame on that fabric, no controller has stopped it (FW-B21), no vote on it is asserted outside the test, and
     all three controllers are functional; else that fabric's phase is skipped and every controller's published phase counter shows the
     skip. The state frames lie outside the hold, so no phase can fail the next window's precondition: the S phase runs as worded
   THE PHASES RUN, fault-free, over 2 cycles (per transceiver and phase; MODEL of the schedule, no figure from a sheet):
     restated schedule, precondition as worded:            every phase of every transceiver 2 times: yes
     round 7's schedule, its precondition as W137 meant it: every phase 2 times: yes
     round 7's schedule, its precondition as worded:       S phases run 0 times (the window after its V phase fails it): MUTANT, FAILS
     DEGRADED, fabric A down at every controller: the restated schedule runs every fabric B phase 2 times and no fabric A phase: yes;
       round 7's runs 0 phases (its precondition needs both fabrics)
   TIMING on printed figures and the drafted rows (each margin less the window clocks' alignment 1.0 ms, DRAFTED, and two crystals'
     drift over a window 4.0 us):
     the hold opens after the last state slot closes                                                                   10.996 ms
     V's votes act before the first peer test frame (the strike chain from the malformed frame at the hold's start)     5.686 ms
     S's own request acts before the first peer test frame                                                              6.986 ms
     the last test frame ends before the hold closes                                                                    6.713 ms
     the release is complete before the next window's first state slot                                                 20.983 ms
     silence takes effect within 10.020 us of the second vote or the own request: the GPIO edge 16.6 ns (speed 00 at 50 pF, DS12110 Table 160
       PRINTED) + the gate's 3.6 ns (tpd at 3.3 V +- 0.3 V, -40 to 85 C, PRINTED) + tMODE 10 us (PRINTED maximum); it ends within 13.01 us
       of the release: SD's 105 kOhm against 20 pF (ASSUMPTION: TI prints no SHDN capacitance; the two diodes' CT 2 pF each PRINTED)
       down to VIL, + tMODE; V's strike: 1.310 ms from the malformed frame to the target's driver off (l9t5_canq.out section 4, MODEL on
       PRINTED parts); the vote line's edge 6.18 ns/V against the gate's 10 ns/V limit at 50 pF (C_VOTE 50 pF, a Layer 10 bound: Ci 4 pF
       and CIO 5 pF PRINTED); a reader's copy of a TXD edge in about 225 ns (2.2 kOhm against 46 pF: ASSUMPTION, a Layer 10 bound)
   THE INTERVAL: one cycle is 12 windows x 100 ms = 1.2000 s; a latent fault of the vote path is exercised within one cycle, judged at its
     window's end, declared when 2 consecutive runs of that phase fail (one corrupted frame never declares one), the verdict exchanged in
     the next window: DETECTED WITHIN 2.60 s of its onset (MODEL on the printed timing and the DRAFTED 100 ms window; round 7's 5.00 s)
     W139's event model of this schedule finds the latest declaration at 2.51 s and, DEGRADED, a fabric B vote stuck low at 2.51 s, both
     within it (l9t5_canq.out section 7); a dead attribution path at 1.71 s (round 7's: NOT FOUND); round 7's precondition as worded: an open
     own-request diode NOT FOUND
   DEGRADED: with one fabric down its phases wait (they need its state frames) and the other fabric's run at the same interval, so every
     element of the surviving fabric keeps the 2.60 s bound; the down fabric's elements are tested again within 2.60 s of its return to
     service, which FW-B21's probe brings within 1.200 s of a repair (l9t5_canq.out section 8); while a controller is out the test waits
     (V needs both peers) and the bound restarts when the quorum is whole
   THE ERROR COUNT: per cycle and fabric a target loses two frames, +16 (S: its test frame; V: its malformed frame, its only frame in that
     hold), against at least 22 successes (its 12 state frames and its test frame in the other 10 windows): bounded and error-active
     (+8 and -1 are ISO 11898-1's, which is not held: ASSUMPTION). Read with its test frame also sent in V, round 8's wording gives +24
     against the same 22 and the count rises a cycle (finding W143-F1): the V phase's malformed frame is the target's only frame there
   DAR = 1 (L9T5-D2, W139-D8), so each failed attempt is one +8, with ES0392 Rev 15 2.24.5's printed workaround (page 48/73):
     "Upon failure, clear the corresponding Tx buffer transmission request bit TRPx of the FDCAN_TXBRP register and set the
     corresponding cancellation finished bit CFx of the FDCAN_TXBCF register, then restart the transmission."
     (W137-F1 answered; the compatibility page's row "firmware does not use DAR" is Layer 6's to restate, W139-F1)
   THE RESTART ROUTE'S PHASES (record l4canen, apply_gen_sch_b_canen.py): in the windows of the fabric A target X, P1 and P2 pulse one
     peer's restart vote on X for 4 ms and V both peers', X reading its restart gate's output; they need only one fabric for the verdict,
     so they keep this interval with either fabric down
   timing and cost hold: yes
   THE SELF-TEST'S OWN FAULTS, element by element (per transceiver; the residuals are named, none defeats the containment alone):
     a vote output, its line or its gate input  stuck low or open              the target cannot be silenced by the vote                      V fails                        within 2.60 s
     a vote output, its line or its gate input  stuck high                     the other peer alone silences the target                       the other peer's P fails       within 2.60 s
     a vote pull-down (10 kOhm)                 short                          as its vote stuck low                                          V fails                        within 2.60 s
     a vote pull-down (10 kOhm)                 open                           the input floats only while its voter is in reset or dark      NOT in service: RESIDUAL       none
     the 2-of-2 gate                            output stuck low               the target cannot be silenced by the vote                      V fails                        within 2.60 s
     the 2-of-2 gate                            output stuck high              the target silenced on that fabric at once (IOHA row 7)        its frames absent              within one window (100 ms)
     the gate's 100 nF                          short                          the target's own rail shorted: the target dark (IOHA row 3)    its frames absent              within one window (100 ms)
     the vote diode                             open                           the target cannot be silenced by the vote                      V fails                        within 2.60 s
     the vote diode                             short                          the gate's low holds SD: the target's own request fails        S fails                        within 2.60 s
     the own-request diode                      open                           the target's own request fails                                 S fails                        within 2.60 s
     the own-request diode                      short                          the request pin's low holds SD: the vote fails                 V fails                        within 2.60 s
     SD's 100 kOhm                              open                           SD rests on the pin's internal pull-down (TI: a fall-back)     NOT in service: RESIDUAL       none
     the transceiver's SHDN input               ignored                        neither the request nor the vote silences                      S and V fail                   within 2.60 s
     a reader's attribution path                dead                           it never strikes the target, so no vote follows a deviation    V fails (V runs it end to end) within 2.60 s
     an isolation resistor                      open                           its reader sees no TXD edge while the frames arrive            continuous reading             within 3 windows (300 ms): every window carries a frame of each controller on each fabric
     an isolation resistor                      short                          a faulty reader could move the buffer's output (not the TXD)   NOT in service: RESIDUAL       none
     a reading pin or its input stage           stuck                          the two readers of one TXD disagree                            continuous reading             within 3 windows (300 ms): every window carries a frame of each controller on each fabric
     a TXD buffer                               stuck or open                  its readers see no edge while its frames arrive                continuous reading             within 3 windows (300 ms): every window carries a frame of each controller on each fabric
     the buffer's 100 nF                        short                          the target's own rail shorted: the target dark (IOHA row 3)    its frames absent              within one window (100 ms)
     a TXD pull-up (10 kOhm)                    short                          the TXD held recessive: no frame on that fabric (IOHA row 7)   its frames absent              within one window (100 ms)
     a TXD pull-up (10 kOhm)                    open                           the TXD on TI's own pull-up only while its controller resets   NOT in service: RESIDUAL       none
     a node's test schedule                     stalled or out of turn         phases fail or counters disagree                               the published phase counter    within one window (100 ms)
     a node's verdict                           wrong (two-faced or corrupted) outvoted: verdicts are taken 2 of 3                            the confirmation               within 2.60 s
   coverage: every one of the 72 parts of the six vote and six observation paths (gates, pull-downs, both diodes, SD's resistor, buffers,
     TXD pull-ups, isolation resistors, the capacitors) is the subject of a row, and every part canmb adds or re-uses is among them: yes;
     the attribution path is a row and the V phase runs it: yes
   the residuals, each needing further faults (W139's rows Q1 to Q4 run each with the fault that makes it act): an open vote pull-down
     acts only while its voter is in reset or dark AND the other peer votes wrongly; a shorted isolation resistor matters only when its
     reader also drives its input, and then reaches the buffer's output, never the TXD; an open SD resistor leaves the transceiver on TI's
     internal pull-down; an open TXD pull-up leaves the TXD on TI's own pull-up only while its controller resets, and a resetting
     controller that drives dominant is then contained by the vote; a voter that resets while asserting gives the gate a slow edge (10
     kOhm against the line) outside the gate's 10 ns/V limit: the output may chatter for that edge, and only while the other peer
     asserts, so it can only end a silence early

